 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, determine the measure of the angles in the given figure.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/447be01c88f859bc.png\" alt=\"Two parallel lines, l subscript 1 and l subscript 2 are intersected by a transversal. The transversal makes four angles labeled 1, 31 degrees, 3, and 4 with the line, l subscript 1. The transversal makes four angles numbered 5, 6, 7, and 8 with the line, l subscript 2. 1, 31 degrees, 7, and 8 are exterior angles. 3, 4, 5, and 6 are interior angles.\">\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532866,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the measure of <span data-math=\"\\measuredangle 1\">\\measuredangle 1</span> and state the reason for your solution.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Angle 1 and the 31° angle are supplementary, so their measures add up to 180°.</p>\n<p>m∡1 = 180° – 31° = 149°</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"m\\measuredangle 1 = {149^ \\circ }\">m\\measuredangle 1 = {149^ \\circ }</span> by supplementary angles with <span data-math=\"\\measuredangle {31^ \\circ }.\">\\measuredangle {31^ \\circ }.</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 532867,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the measure of <span data-math=\"\\measuredangle 3\">\\measuredangle 3</span> and state the reason for your solution.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Angle 3 and the 31° angle are vertical angles. Vertical angles have equal measures.</p>\n<p>m∡3 = 31°</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"m\\measuredangle 3 = {31^ \\circ }\">m\\measuredangle 3 = {31^ \\circ }</span> by vertical angles with the angle measuring <span data-math=\"{31^ \\circ }.\">{31^ \\circ }.</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 532868,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the measure of  <span data-math=\"\\measuredangle 5\">\\measuredangle 5</span> and state the reason for your solution.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Angle 1 and the 31° angle are supplementary, so their measures add up to 180°.</p>\n<p>The measure of angle 1 = 180° – 31° = 149°</p>\n<p>Angle 5 and angle 1 are corresponding angles, so they have equal measures.</p>\n<p>m∡5 = 149°</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"m\\measuredangle 5 = {149^ \\circ }\">m\\measuredangle 5 = {149^ \\circ }</span> by corresponding angles with <span data-math=\"\\measuredangle 1.\">\\measuredangle 1.</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
